.TH MPD-SET-PERMISSIONS 1 "September 2025" "hifiberry-mpd" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
mpd-set-permissions \- set ACL permissions for MPD directories
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mpd-set-permissions
.I username
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mpd-set-permissions
sets Access Control List (ACL) permissions for MPD directories to allow a specific user to read and write to MPD's data directories. This is useful when multiple users need access to MPD's music library and playlists.
.PP
The script configures ACL permissions for the following directories:
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
/var/lib/mpd
.IP \(bu 2
/var/lib/mpd/music
.IP \(bu 2
/var/lib/mpd/playlists
.RE
.PP
The script sets both regular ACL permissions and default ACL permissions so that new files and directories inherit the correct permissions.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.I username
The name of the user to grant read/write access to MPD directories. The user must exist on the system.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Grant MPD directory access to user 'alice':
.B mpd-set-permissions alice
.SH DEPENDENCIES
This script requires the
.B acl
package to be installed, which provides the
.BR setfacl (1)
and
.BR getfacl (1)
commands.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /var/lib/mpd
Main MPD data directory
.TP
.I /var/lib/mpd/music
MPD music library directory
.TP
.I /var/lib/mpd/playlists
MPD playlists directory
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mpd (1),
.BR setfacl (1),
.BR getfacl (1),
.BR configure-mpd (1)
.SH AUTHOR
HiFiBerry <support@hifiberry.com>